You can use the focus() method in JavaScript to focus on an element found by getElementsByTagName.

Here is an example:
```
var elements = document.getElementsByTagName("input");
elements[0].focus();  // Focus on the first input element
```
This will focus on the first input element on the page.

If you want to focus on an element by its id, you can use getElementsById instead:
```
var element = document.getElementById("myId");
element.focus();
```
If you have multiple elements with the same tag name, you can loop through them and focus on the one you want:
```
var elements = document.getElementsByTagName("input");
for (var i = 0; i < elements.length; i++) {
  if (elements[i].id === "myId") {
    elements[i].focus();
    break;
  }
}
```
Note that the focus() method will only work if the element is a form element (such as a input, select, or textarea), or an element that can be focused (such as a link).

Also, you can use querySelector to get the element, it's more efficient than getElementsByTagName
